 as the diagnosis: (1) The CT findings exactly match the pathognomonic 'whirl sign' description; (2) The patient's demographic (86-year-old woman) fits the classic epidemiology; (3) The swirling sign is not characteristic of other biliary pathologies; (4) The acute presentation aligns with the emergent nature of volvulus requiring surgical intervention. This information effectively rules out other options while confirming volvulus as the most likely diagnosis.\"\n}\n```",
