V is a strongly indicated procedure for this patient, it is not one of the provided multiple-choice options. Among the given options, intravitreal antimicrobial injection is the absolute minimum required intervention and is always performed, whether as a standalone procedure or immediately preceding a vitrectomy.\"\n    },\n    \"diagnostic_application\": \"This retrieved knowledge conclusively validates the selection of 'Intravitreal antimicrobial injections' (Option 1). The guidelines and evidence confirm that this is a non-negotiable, evidence-based step in managing confirmed bacterial endophthalmitis. It is the most direct and critical intervention to save the eye and any remaining vision. The other options are either contraindicated (steroids without antibiotic control), insufficient (topical agents), or not indicated based on the information given (IOL removal). The fact that a vitrectomy is also indicated but not an option does not diminish the necessity of the intravitreal injection; it is the foundational treatment upon which all other surgical management is built.\"\n}\n```",
