y_of_microaneurysms\": \"The visceral arteriography showing multiple microaneurysms in digestive visceral and renal arteries is highly specific for PAN and effectively rules out ANCA-associated vasculitides as the primary diagnosis.\",\n        \"role_of_negative_serology\": \"The negative ANCA and ANA tests exclude the most common autoimmune vasculitis mimics (GPA, MPA, lupus), strongly supporting PAN as the diagnosis in the context of characteristic angiographic findings.\",\n        \"pet_scan_in_vasculitis\": \"The PET scan showing increased metabolic activity in small and medium vessel walls provided the first objective evidence of vasculitis, prompting the definitive angiographic study that confirmed the diagnosis of PAN.\"\n    }\n}\n```",
