e sons do not inherit the mutation; option 3 is inaccurate as daughters have a 100% chance, not 50%; option 4, while true for women with FXTAS, is not directly relevant to the inheritance from a male proband.\",\n    \"selected_option\": \"All daughters of men with FXTAS are obligate FMRI premutation carriers\",\n    \"confidence\": 0.95,\n    \"self_questions\": [\"Is there any scenario where a daughter might not inherit the premutation due to rare genetic events like recombination?\", \"How does the size of the premutation in the father affect the risk for daughters developing FXTAS?\"],\n    \"needs_retrieval\": false\n}",
